<objective>
Tracer: one checkout row removed end to end over REST. `Manager::preview_removal` and `Manager::remove_rows` wrap `baude_core::removal::{preview_removal, remove}` with the runtime custody, recheck-under-lock and rollback posture the TUI established in Phase 20, and `api.rs` exposes them as `POST /removals/preview` and `POST /removals` with the daemon's plain-text error convention. The slice touches every layer this phase modifies in the daemon (Manager, api router, state file) and proves the shape before the expansion plans add row kinds, SSE, the hierarchy projection and the two clients.

Decision map for this phase (CONTEXT.md bullets in order): D-01 route family and RemovalTarget body; D-02 RemovalReport verbatim as 200 JSON; D-03 plain-text error statuses 404/409/500/503; D-04 execute echoes the preview sets and the daemon rechecks under the lock; D-05 /events broadcast; D-06 rows_removed event carries the report; D-07 publish after persist inside the lock; D-08 PWA and TUI drop rows by key; D-09 /rows projection and SessionInfo.checkout_key; D-10 PWA remove on all four kinds; D-11 daemon admission through the shared suppression helper; D-12 TUI D on a remote row becomes a real action; D-13 openModal reuse with the TUI sections; D-14 409 re-renders in place; D-15 500/503 keep the modal open with Retry; D-16 repository parent lists every child by name and branch.

This plan implements D-01, D-02, D-03 and D-04 for the checkout kind. Execute body decision: the body of `POST /removals` is the preview `RemovalReport` JSON echoed verbatim, so the PWA and the TUI resend exactly what they rendered; the daemon reads `target`, `rows_removed`, `runtimes_killed` and `paths_deleted` from it and ignores the rest (resolves RESEARCH assumption A3 without a second wire type).

Purpose: the single source of truth for removal stays `baude-core`; the daemon owns handles, lock, persist and status mapping only.
Output: compiled Manager and api code with HTTP tests that drive a live `sleep 30` runtime through preview and execute against an isolated fixture repository and state file.
</objective>

