<threat_model>
## Trust Boundaries

| Boundary | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| tailnet client to bauded | Untrusted JSON bodies for /removals and /removals/preview cross here; no auth layer by design (api.rs:1-2, deferred per CONTEXT) |
| bauded to filesystem | The removal deletes managed worktree directories and rewrites the daemon state file |

## STRIDE Threat Register

| Threat ID | Category | Component | Severity | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
|-----------|----------|-----------|----------|-------------|-----------------|
| T-21-01 | Tampering | execute_removal body (echoed RemovalReport) | high | mitigate | The daemon never acts on echoed paths or runtimes: it recomputes preview_removal under the lock and only compares the three sets; paths come from repository_state alone. 21-03 adds the test that echoes a bogus paths_deleted entry and proves nothing is deleted |
| T-21-02 | Denial of Service | Manager lock held across kill and disk stages | medium | accept | Same posture as DELETE /sessions/{id} today; the kill stage is bounded by the core teardown timeout and the repository reservation refuses a concurrent activation rather than deadlocking |
| T-21-SC | Tampering | npm/pip/cargo installs | high | mitigate | No package is added in this plan; package-legitimacy gate plus a blocking human checkpoint would apply to any [ASSUMED]/[SUS] crate |
</threat_model>

