  <action>
    Add `"sync"` to the tokio feature list in `bauded/Cargo.toml` (an existing audited dependency; no new package). In `manager.rs` add `#[derive(Clone, Debug)] pub enum DaemonEvent { RowsRemoved(RemovalReport) }`, a field `events: tokio::sync::broadcast::Sender<DaemonEvent>` created with capacity 64 in `Manager::new`, `pub fn subscribe_events(&self) -> broadcast::Receiver<DaemonEvent>`, and in `remove_rows` on the `Ok(report)` arm, after the `runtime_checkouts` cleanup and before returning, `let _ = self.events.send(DaemonEvent::RowsRemoved(report.clone()))` (a `SendError` only means no receiver and is not a failure). In `api.rs` add `.route("/events", get(events))` whose handler takes `State(state)`, calls `lock(&state).subscribe_events()` before building the stream (so the receiver exists the moment the response is returned), then yields `Event::default().event("rows_removed").data(serde_json::to_string(&report))` for each `Ok(DaemonEvent::RowsRemoved(report))`, `continue`s on `RecvError::Lagged`, and ends on `Closed`; keep-alive via `KeepAlive::default()` like the other streams. Add a test helper `async fn next_sse_message(body, timeout) -> Option<(String, String)>` returning event name and data for the first complete message that is not a comment; it is the Wave 0 SSE helper RESEARCH asked for. Commit as `feat(21-04): add daemon-wide events stream with rows_removed`.
