Give the PWA the same remove the TUI has, through the daemon. The pure parts (report to modal sections, report to row drops, report to notice text) live in a new plain-script module `removal.js` that also exports for Node so `node --test` covers them against hand-built reports the way Phase 20 unit-tested `remove_project_confirmation_lines`. `app.js` wires `/rows`, the modal, the failure posture and the `/events` subscription. Native `confirm()` is not used.

Purpose: API-03 end to end, with the confirmation describing exactly what the daemon reported.
