  </read_first>
  <behavior>
    - `confirmationView(report, rows)` returns `{ title, sections: [{ label, lines }] }` where `title` names the kind from `report.target` ("repository", "checkout", "standalone session"), `rows dropped` lists each `rows_removed` entry as the row's name from the `/rows` structure plus its branch when it has one (D-16), `runtimes killed` has the count in its label and one line per runtime naming the row, `paths deleted` and `paths kept` list exactly the report's arrays and nothing else, `already removed` lists each `report.already_removed` path so the user sees it is already gone from disk and it is never shown under paths deleted, and `clearings` lists each entry of `report.cleared` by its kind and path; `report.readers_parked` is always empty in a preview and is not rendered by the modal; empty sections are omitted except rows dropped.
    - `dropRows(rows, report)` returns a new `/rows` structure without any repository, checkout or standalone whose key appears in `report.rows_removed`, leaving a repository in place when only a child was removed.
    - `removalNotice(report)` returns the TUI's footer wording shape with counts of rows, runtimes and paths, and `clearingFailures(report)` returns the failed clearing descriptions for the toast.
    - Tests cover a checkout preview, a repository parent with two children, a standalone row, a report with a failed clearing, a report with no runtimes, and a report whose `already_removed` holds one path asserting it renders under `already removed` and never under paths deleted. Every fixture report carries every field of the serde shape above, in the snake_case form the daemon emits: `target`, `planned`, `rows_removed`, `runtimes_killed`, `paths_deleted`, `paths_kept`, `already_removed`, `readers_parked`, `persistence`, `cleared`, `clearing_failures`, with `RowKey`, `KilledRuntime`, `PersistenceOutcome`, `ClearedItem` and `ClearingFailure` items in the shapes removal.rs serialises; a fixture with a field the daemon never emits is a defect in the fixture, not a passing test.
  </behavior>
