  </read_first>
  <behavior>
    - `RemoteInfo` gains `#[serde(default)] pub checkout_key: Option<CheckoutKey>`; the existing deserialisation of a payload without the field still succeeds (existing tests).
    - `RemotePoller::preview_removal(&self, target: RemovalTarget) -> Result<RemovalReport, String>` posts the target JSON and parses the 200 body; non-2xx yields `Err` with the status and plain body.
    - `RemotePoller::execute_removal(&self, report: &RemovalReport) -> Result<RemoteRemovalOutcome, String>`: 200 yields `Removed(report)`, 409 parses the body as a report and yields `Recheck(fresh)`, any other status yields `Err("daemon said {code}: {body}")`.
    - `RemotePoller::drop_rows(&self, report: &RemovalReport)` removes every snapshot session whose `checkout_key` is one of the report's `RowKey::Checkout` entries.
    - The events thread started by `RemotePoller::start` connects `GET /events` with `ureq` using `timeout_connect` only, parses `event:` and `data:` lines terminated by a blank line, calls `drop_rows` on `rows_removed`, ignores comments and other events, and reconnects after `POLL_SECS` when the connection ends.
    - Tests in `remote.rs`: a `#[cfg(test)] pub(crate) mod test_double` with `fn serve(script: Vec<(method, path, status, content_type, body)>) -> (base_url, JoinHandle)` on a `TcpListener` bound to `127.0.0.1:0`, answering one request per script entry in order, plus a variant that streams an SSE body with one `rows_removed` frame then closes; tests `remote_preview_removal_returns_the_report`, `remote_execute_removal_maps_409_to_recheck`, `remote_execute_removal_surfaces_503_text`, `remote_drop_rows_removes_sessions_by_checkout_key`, `remote_events_frame_drops_rows_from_snapshot` (poll thread pointed at a port that refuses so the double owns the data).
  </behavior>
  <action>
    RED first with `todo!()` bodies and a failing run recorded in the SUMMARY. Keep `REQUEST_TIMEOUT` for the two POSTs. For the events thread build the request with `ureq::AgentBuilder::new().timeout_connect(REQUEST_TIMEOUT).build()` and no read timeout, take `into_reader()` wrapped in a `BufReader`, and parse lines. Make `RemotePoller::start` spawn the events thread alongside the poll thread; add `#[cfg(test)] fn start_without_events(base)` so existing TUI tests that point at a refusing port do not spin a second reconnecting thread. The double must accept any request headers and body length and answer exactly as scripted so that a wrong path or method surfaces as a test failure, never as a tolerant match. Commit as `feat(21-06): add daemon removal calls and events subscription to the remote client`.
  </action>
  <verify>
    <automated>cargo test -p baude remote::tests::remote_ -- --test-threads=1 > /tmp/baude-21-06-remote.log 2>&1; STATUS=$?; grep -E 'running [1-9][0-9]* tests?' /tmp/baude-21-06-remote.log; test $STATUS -eq 0 && grep -qE 'running [1-9][0-9]* tests?' /tmp/baude-21-06-remote.log</automated>
  </verify>
  <done>The remote client previews, executes, maps 409 and errors, drops rows by key, and consumes the events stream, all proven against the scripted double.</done>
