<threat_model>
## Trust Boundaries

| Boundary | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| TUI to daemon over the tailnet | The TUI sends targets and echoed reports and renders daemon-supplied names and paths in the terminal |

## STRIDE Threat Register

| Threat ID | Category | Component | Severity | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
|-----------|----------|-----------|----------|-------------|-----------------|
| T-21-11 | Denial of Service | events subscriber thread reconnect loop | low | mitigate | Reconnect waits POLL_SECS between attempts and shares the poller's lifetime; tests use start_without_events so refusing ports never spin |
| T-21-12 | Tampering | daemon-supplied strings rendered into the modal | low | accept | The renderer already truncates and displays report strings as text; the terminal does not interpret them |
| T-21-SC | Tampering | npm/pip/cargo installs | high | mitigate | No package is added; package-legitimacy gate plus a blocking human checkpoint would apply to any [ASSUMED]/[SUS] crate |
</threat_model>

