codex
The shared core operation supports the proposed daemon wrapper. One important detail: on an error, it restores row ownership, but runtimes may already be stopped and worktrees may already be deleted. I’m checking how the retry flow handles that, along with whether polling can overwrite SSE-driven row drops.
