.planning/phases/21-daemon-and-pwa-parity/21-03-PLAN.md:32:Harden the 21-01 execute path against the three ways it can go wrong and prove the daemon never trusts the echoed body. Drift between preview and execute returns 409 with the fresh report (D-04); kill and persist failures map to 500 and 503 with handles restored and rows intact (D-03); a bogus `paths_deleted` entry in the execute body is ignored because the daemon recomputes everything under the lock (T-21-01 from 21-01). The TUI's `remove_project_` tests in Phase 20 plan 04 are the template: same forced failures, same expectations, over HTTP.
