.planning/phases/21-daemon-and-pwa-parity/21-01-PLAN.md:32:Tracer: one checkout row removed end to end over REST. `Manager::preview_removal` and `Manager::remove_rows` wrap `baude_core::removal::{preview_removal, remove}` with the runtime custody, recheck-under-lock and rollback posture the TUI established in Phase 20, and `api.rs` exposes them as `POST /removals/preview` and `POST /removals` with the daemon's plain-text error convention. The slice touches every layer this phase modifies in the daemon (Manager, api router, state file) and proves the shape before the expansion plans add row kinds, SSE, the hierarchy projection and the two clients.
.planning/phases/21-daemon-and-pwa-parity/21-01-PLAN.md:36:This plan implements D-01, D-02, D-03 and D-04 for the checkout kind. Execute body decision: the body of `POST /removals` is the preview `RemovalReport` JSON echoed verbatim, so the PWA and the TUI resend exactly what they rendered; the daemon reads `target`, `rows_removed`, `runtimes_killed` and `paths_deleted` from it and ignores the rest (resolves RESEARCH assumption A3 without a second wire type).
.planning/phases/21-daemon-and-pwa-parity/21-01-PLAN.md:39:Output: compiled Manager and api code with HTTP tests that drive a live `sleep 30` runtime through preview and execute against an isolated fixture repository and state file.
.planning/phases/21-daemon-and-pwa-parity/21-01-PLAN.md:56:Noun now primary: `baude_core::removal::{RemovalTarget, RemovalReport}` is the one removal contract; the TUI (Phase 20), the daemon REST surface and the PWA are three callers of it. Decision: no-change. Phase 18 already promoted the shared operation to core; this phase adds callers, not a second representation. A later phase that hand-rolls a daemon-side row set instead of calling core would be the regression; the recheck tests in 21-03 compare the daemon's response against `preview_removal` output, which goes red if that happens.
