.planning/phases/21-daemon-and-pwa-parity/21-01-PLAN.md:79:    Manager (D-01, D-02, D-04): add `pub fn preview_removal(&self, target: RemovalTarget) -> Result<RemovalReport, RemovalError>` delegating to `baude_core::removal::preview_removal(&self.repository_state, target)`. Add `pub enum RemoveRowsError { Drift(RemovalReport), Removal(RemovalError), Blocked(persist::SaveError) }` with Display. Add `pub fn remove_rows(&mut self, previewed: &RemovalReport) -> Result<RemovalReport, RemoveRowsError>` that: returns `Blocked` when `persistence_blocked` (same message `create` uses); reserves the target's repository through `repository_reservations` the way the TUI's `reserve_removal_target` does, holding the returned `RepositoryReservation` guard for the whole call. `RepositoryReservations::reserve` at baude-core/src/lifecycle.rs:2839 returns `Err(LifecycleOutcome::Busy { repository })` when another mutation holds that repository; add a `Busy(RepositoryKey)` variant to `RemoveRowsError` for it, and the handler maps `Busy` to 503 with the plain-text body `repository busy: <path>`, the same status family as `Blocked`, never 409, because D-03 reserves 409 bodies for the fresh-report JSON. Nothing is killed or saved when the reservation is busy; recomputes `preview_removal(previewed.target)` under the caller's lock and returns `Drift(fresh)` when `rows_removed`, `runtimes_killed` or `paths_deleted` differ from `previewed` (the three sets the TUI compares); moves the live `Session` for every `RowKey::Checkout` in the fresh report out of `self.sessions` into `Vec<RowRuntime>` through `runtime_checkouts` (mirror `collect_row_runtimes`; `RowKey::Repository` and `RowKey::Standalone` carry no daemon runtime); calls `baude_core::removal::remove(&mut self.repository_state, target, &mut runtimes, save)` where `save` is a closure built like the TUI's: when `!self.persist` it returns Ok without touching disk, in `cfg(test)` with `persistence_target_for_test` set it calls `persist::save_current_at_test(root, file_name, file, atomic_failure_for_test, None)`, otherwise `persist::save_for_workspace_status(STATE_BASE, baude_core::workspace::active(), file)`; on `Err` restores every runtime into `self.sessions` in id order (mirror `restore_row_runtimes`), clears `atomic_failure_for_test` in tests, and returns `Removal(error)`; on `Ok` removes the `runtime_checkouts` entries for every removed checkout, removes and notifies `permission_notify` for every consumed session id, sets `persistence_dirty` to whether `report.persistence` is `SavedDegraded`, and returns the report. Do not route through `Manager::remove` or `teardown_retained_runtime`: this is the Phase 18 force path, not the close protocol (removal.rs comment above `remove`). Add `#[cfg(test)] pub(crate) fn checkout_key_for_runtime_for_test(&self, id: u64) -> Option<CheckoutKey>`.
.planning/phases/21-daemon-and-pwa-parity/21-01-PLAN.md:81:    api.rs (D-01, D-03): register `.route("/removals/preview", post(preview_removal))` and `.route("/removals", post(execute_removal))` in `router`. `preview_removal` extracts `Json<RemovalTarget>` and returns `Json<RemovalReport>`; `execute_removal` extracts `Json<RemovalReport>` and returns `Json<RemovalReport>`. Add `fn removal_error(error: RemoveRowsError) -> axum::response::Response` mapping `Drift(report)` to 409 with `Json(report)` (the one JSON error body, D-03), `Removal(UnknownTarget)` to 404 plain text, `Removal(Persist)` and `Blocked` to 503 plain text, every other `Removal` arm (RuntimeSurvived, DiskRemoval, RuntimeHandleMissing, RuntimeIdentityMismatch, Validation) to 500 plain text, each body being the error's Display. A malformed body is axum's own Json rejection; do not add a custom one. Put the tests in the inline `mod tests` of `api.rs` (discretion: one module, next to the harness they reuse).
