The client review turned up three more gaps: both pollers can apply a response fetched before removal after SSE has dropped the row; a fresh 409 report can include children missing from the PWA’s name lookup; and the “live runtime” fixtures use bare `sleep 30`, which exits when the daemon appends permission flags. I’m finishing the per-plan risks and suggested fixes.
