     1	# baude
     2	
     3	Cargo workspace: `baude-core` (no UI deps), `baude` (ratatui TUI), `bauded` (axum daemon).
     4	
     5	## Gate
     6	
     7	Run `scripts/gate.sh` before every push. It is the `check` job of `ci.yml`, in order, with unpiped
     8	exit codes. `scripts/gate.sh --linux` runs the same gate in `rust:1-bookworm` as uid 1000; use it
     9	for anything touching platform code (`cfg`, procfs, file timing), because macOS has hidden
    10	Linux-only defects before. Never judge a gate step by piping it to `tail` or `grep` and reading `$?`.
    11	
    12	## Releases
    13	
    14	release-please owns versions, tags and the GitHub Release. Merging conventional commits to `main`
    15	opens a release PR: patch bumps auto-merge once required checks pass, minor bumps after a soak,
    16	and majors are merged by hand. `main` is protected, so every change lands by PR.
    17	
    18	Never nest parentheses in a commit body, squash message or PR title. release-please silently
    19	skips such a commit and no release PR opens. `scripts/check-commit-message.sh` catches it; enable
    20	it locally with `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`.
    21	
